# What Muse Spark identified: pharmacy / medicines

Catalogue writes BRAND + strength + galenic form + pack: e.g. 10MG CP PELLI SEC B/30, 250MG/5ML SP FL 60ML, 0.1% COLLYRE FL 5ML. Strengths use MG/G/MCG/MUI/UI/% with comma decimals, single (10MG) or double/triple (500MG/65MG, 500/62.5MG, 1G/125MG, 0.2G/0.5G/100ML). Forms are abbreviated: CP, GLES/GELS, SP, SUSP BUV, SOL, GTTES, PDRE SACHT, AMP, INJ, SUPP, OVUL, CREME/GEL/PDE/T. Packs are B/XX, BT, S/30, T/15G for tubes and FL XXML volumes. Two products of one brand differ by dosage, form/pack and AD/ENF or LP.

## First-pass blocks

- **strength** ON — many products are defined by two-value dosage 500mg/65mg, 1g/125mg, 80mg/12.5mg, 250mg/5ml that must become one dose token
  - evidence: reads 87 catalogue names differently; products that read alike 13 → 10
- **units_glue** ON — catalogue mixes 10MG and 10 MG, 60ML and 60 ML, 15G and 15 G; number+mg/ml/g/ui must be glued to match
  - evidence: reads 0 catalogue names differently; products that read alike 10 → 10
- **pack_count** ON — pack is B/30, BT100, BTE, S/30, B/14, B/28 that must become one x30 token to distinguish same dosage different box size
  - evidence: reads 303 catalogue names differently; products that read alike 10 → 5

