## Search method

**BM25** (BM25)

## Rules (rule engineer and attributes)

- R-0014 [shadow] "ss" or "s s" is the variant "ss", in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; a variant stated on one side only, or a different one, is never the same product. — by rule-engineer
- R-0013 [shadow] "oro disp" is written as "orod". — by rule-engineer
- R-0012 [rejected] "enfant" means "enf". — by rule-engineer (resolves only 1 new line(s) and brings 0 closer; the gate needs 2 resolved or 6 closer)
- R-0011 [shadow] "flc" means "fl". — by rule-engineer
- R-0010 [shadow] "cr" means "creme". — by rule-engineer
- R-0009 [rejected] "sol buv" means "susp buv". — by rule-engineer (resolves only 1 new line(s) and brings 0 closer; the gate needs 2 resolved or 6 closer)
- R-0008 [shadow] "sol inj" means "inj". — by rule-engineer
- R-0007 [shadow] "comp" or "comprimes" or "comprime" or "compr" means "cp". — by rule-engineer
- R-0006 [live] "pel" or "enro" or "pell" or "pelli" or "pellicule" or "pelliculaire" or "enrob" or "enrobe" describes a product but never tells two products apart. — by rule-engineer
