## Calibrations

- **calibration after 10 invoices** (134 seen + 45 unseen lines): 57/134 right with no AI (43 %), 1 wrong → 83/134 right with no AI (62 %), 1 wrong; accepted 3, rejected 26; search: 1.5·BM25 (brand ×3) + 0.6·trigrams: right product in the top 8 for 91.8 % of lines (MRR 0.91) → BM25: 85.8 % in the top 8 (MRR 0.85); engineer rules []; $0.2165. Spark: Lines use COMP/CPR/COMPRIMES for CP, GELULES for GLES, SIROP/SIR/SRP for SP or generic, plus glued doses and bare 50/100 dosages.
- **calibration after 20 invoices** (293 seen + 98 unseen lines): 183/293 right with no AI (62 %), 1 wrong → 187/293 right with no AI (64 %), 1 wrong; accepted 1, rejected 10; search: BM25: right product in the top 8 for 85.7 % of lines (MRR 0.85) → BM25: 85.0 % in the top 8 (MRR 0.84); engineer rules [R-0005 R-0006 R-0007 R-0008]; $0.2788. Spark: Lines use CPR/COMP/COMPRIMES SIR/SIROP CRM GELULES FLC SACH VIT/AD/ENFANTS variants of catalogue CP SP CREME GLES FLACON SACHET VITAMINE ADULTES ENF plus glued BREQUAL50 and 60CP and bare 50/250 doses.
- **calibration after 30 invoices** (436 seen + 146 unseen lines): 300/436 right with no AI (69 %), 1 wrong → 300/436 right with no AI (69 %), 1 wrong; accepted 0, rejected 7; search: BM25: right product in the top 8 for 87.8 % of lines (MRR 0.87) → BM25: 87.8 % in the top 8 (MRR 0.87); engineer rules [R-0010 R-0011 R-0013 R-0014]; $0.8952. Spark: catalogue uses short forms CP PELLI GLES SP SACHET/SACHT FL that lines write as CPR PELLIC SIR CRM COMPRIMES GELULES SACH FLc, plus bare doses 500/62.5MG and glued BREQUAL50/250

